<Legal
  title="Preview Subprocessors"
  description="Convex, Cloudflare and WorkOS provide the backend, hosting and sign-in for Volli’s invite-only preview."
  path="/legal/subprocessors/"
>
  <p>
    These are the service providers Volli uses to process data for the invite-only 0.3
    preview. This is a preview list, not a list of planned integrations.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Convex, Inc.</strong> — backend database and server functions. Processes
      account, Workspace, membership, board, configuration and Session records,
      credentials you choose to store, connected-account and repository metadata, and
      device and runner metadata needed for the service.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> — website and docs hosting, and object storage for
      synced Session transcript bodies and agent logs. Also relays model requests and
      responses, including prompts and code, when a backend-held API connection is used.
      Processes stored history, relayed data and connection information for requests to
      its services.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>WorkOS, Inc.</strong> — AuthKit sign-in and authentication sessions. Processes
      profile and identity information, email, and sign-in connection and session metadata.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    These providers may process data outside Canada, including in the United States and
    on global networks. We make no region-specific storage promise for this preview.
  </p>
  <h2>Services you choose</h2>
  <p>
    Model providers, gateways, git hosts, MCP servers and other tools you connect are
    services you direct, not additional Volli preview subprocessors. They can receive
    prompts, code or other data you send, under your agreements with them. Your own Mac
    runs the preview's agent tools.
  </p>
  <p>
    We will update this list before adding a provider that processes preview data.
    Questions or privacy requests can be sent privately through your preview invitation.
  </p>
</Legal>
